	(text "The worst noise in the system\nis from the inverter at 12kHz\n\nThese signals change quite\nslowly in comparison, so the\ncut-off frequency can be low\n\nFilters can be bypassed\nwith a 0R resistor and no\ncapacitor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 42.545 98.425 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "17322cbc-6e74-4d1a-9e2d-8c301887d31d")
	)
	(text "Planned changes:\n- check if optoiso is the best choice\n- swap for a much smaller package\n- double number of inputs\n\nWhy:\n- future proofing\n- space will be an issue on this board, so \n  trying to keep things neat\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 261.112 45.847 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 153 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3a8a6816-3ecb-4d4d-9fc0-d08dd8c5d1bf")
	)
	(text "Planned changes:\n- check if optoiso is the best choice\n- swap for a much smaller package\n- double number of inputs\n\nWhy:\n- future proofing\n- space will be an issue on this board, so \n  trying to keep things neat\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.322 87.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 153 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4ce56bbb-4aff-4258-bea8-bb892a7443c2")
	)
	(text "Planned changes:\n- double number of channels\n- proper input clamping\n- use 2.5vref\n- make input voltage configurable via jumpers\n- add spice sims\n- add more filter stages\n- unify grounds\n\nBecause:\n- make readings nicer (anti-aliasing)\n- protect from transience\n- any sensor can be connected up to each channel\n  so more cusomisable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 155.829 50.546 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 153 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7198a2c6-14f5-4c83-80da-2fc22726ce50")
	)
	(text "IC Power and Unused "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.775 41.275 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7422ec3b-d38b-46cd-a66a-f9b5309f3eb9")
	)
	(text "These resistor values assume\nthe input signal will occupy\nthe full 12V range, which is \nnot true in practice\n\nCalibrate resistors appropriately\nduring testing!"
